WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.290
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.220
Trolls, the latest film from DreamWorks Animation,
takes us on a journey through the world of

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:12.261
these all-hugging, all-singing, and all-dancing
cute little shiny happy creatures as they

00:00:12.261 --> 00:00:17.900
try to avoid being captured by the extremely
gloomy ogre-like Bergens, who can only experience

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.100
happiness by gobbling up Trolls.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.960
The story is quite straightforward and follows
an odd couple, the always cheery and optimistic

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.800
Poppy and the downbeat and ever-anxious Branch,
as they somewhat reluctantly set out together

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.379
to save their fellow brightly coloured beings
from ending up in the Bergens' stomachs.

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:38.800
With Pitch Perfect's Anna Kendrick voicing
Poppy, Justin Timberlake playing Branch, and

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.879
New Girl's Zooey Deschanel as the Bergen scullery
maid Bridget, the filmmakers would have been

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:45.690
mad not to make the most of their cast's singing
talents.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.949
So, you can expect plenty of musical scenes
and song-and-dance numbers, the majority of

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.640
which fit pretty nicely within the tale being
told.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.460
The toys the movie's based on were actually
popular at various points from the 1960s through

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:02.019
to the 90s, so fittingly the soundtrack is
mostly filled with tunes from those eras,

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:06.299
including some classic disco tracks and power
ballads, as well as some new pop songs.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.342
If you like many of the songs which the cast
covers, then you'll likely find yourself in

00:01:09.342 --> 00:01:13.060
a good mood and the right place to enjoy the
movie overall.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.869
But it's the animation where the film really
shines.

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:21.390
There's an incredible tactile, textured quality
to the whole film, and particularly the Trolls

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.390
themselves.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.289
Directors Mike Mitchell and Walt Dohrn and
their animators have really outdone themselves

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:31.000
capturing the felty, fuzziness of the Trolls
and their world, which is essentially a crazy

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.600
blast of colours and glitter.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.390
And there's an especially lovely sequence
where Poppy wanders through the forest and

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.070
comes across all sorts of weird beasts and
plant life.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:43.899
Sure, the story and characters don't have
the complexity or the wide range of pop culture

00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:48.189
easter eggs we get from the likes of Pixar
or the best of Disney or Dreamworks itself.

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:52.810
And it's clear where Jonathan Aibel and Glenn
Berger's screenplay is going from the start.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.790
And, yes, the movie does put its message front
and centre on several occasions.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:01.310
Still, though we've seen characters like these
before and the story certainly borrows from

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.219
the likes of The Hobbit, Cinderella, and Cyrano
de Bergerac, or if you prefer Roxanne, the

00:02:06.219 --> 00:02:10.940
movie is perfectly enjoyable, sweet, and decent
fun that moves along at a good pace and knows

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.600
to quit by the 90-minute mark while it's still
ahead.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.120
Make no mistake: Trolls is squarely aimed
at younger kids, but there are some adult-tinged

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.190
moments, and the quality of the animation,
the music, and some of its humour means it

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.610
does have potential for adult audiences too.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:30.440
And, of course, it's entirely possible some
grown-ups may identify with aspects of Branch's

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.360
less-than-rosy attitude to life, which, while
it makes him an outlier among his joy-filled

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.930
fellow Trolls, acts as a nice counterbalance
to the Trolls' never-ending wildly enthusiastic

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.830
nature, which some adults might find a little
jarring otherwise.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:50.560
To sum up: Trolls creates a beautifully textured
fuzzy world packed with colour and sparkle.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.290
The movie's clear storyline and simple message,
wrapped up in bright packaging, makes it ideal

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.450
for younger kids.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.060
And while it's unlikely to make your list
of unforgettable films, it will likely keep

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:04.390
you and definitely any young ones entertained
while you're watching.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.580
So, I'm giving Trolls 3 out of 5 Flicks.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.530
